author: pm-github
body: "Related PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/pull/152\n\n# [P2] Standalone SVG renders solid black in Inkscape after colors become CSS variables\n\nPR #152 replaces literal SVG colors with `var(--pm-...)` values without literal paint fallbacks. Inkscape 1.4 does not resolve those custom properties, so both the background and foreground become black and the chart is unreadable. The same synthetic input renders legibly before this change.\n\nAffected head: `130c2f0b06a28dabe08aa058c7ea75d1d585ccc1` ([index.ts:2114–2121](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/blob/130c2f0b06a28dabe08aa058c7ea75d1d585ccc1/index.ts#L2114-L2121), with the same paint pattern throughout `renderSvg`). Base: `cc4e5d4d1c0e390722f982ee80833d7e54deec4b`.\n\n## Self-contained reproduction\n\nPrerequisites: a checkout at the affected head with its normal dependencies installed, supported Node, Inkscape 1.4, and Python 3 with Pillow for the optional pixel oracle. Run from the repository root after the normal build:\n\n```sh\nnpm run build\nREPRO_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\nenv -i PATH=\"$PATH\" HOME=\"$REPRO_HOME\" TZ=UTC DO_NOT_TRACK=1 PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1 PM_SENTRY_DISABLED=1 node --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { renderSvg } from './dist/index.js';\n\nconst start = new Date('2026-10-12T00:00:00Z');\nconst opts = {\n  weeks: 1, width: 320, groupBy: 'type', statusFilter: 'all',\n  today: start, criticalPath: false, criticalOnly: false,\n  schedule: false, defaultDuration: 5, progress: true, milestones: [],\n};\nconst rows = ['open', 'in_progress', 'blocked', 'closed', 'canceled'].map((status, i) => ({\n  item: {\n    id: `item-${i}`, title: `Review ${status}`, status,\n    type: 'Task', priority: 1, deadline: '2026-10-16',\n  },\n  group: 'Task', startWeek: 0, endWeek: 0,\n  start, end: new Date('2026-10-16T00:00:00Z'),\n  critical: false, overdue: i === 0, progress: 50,\n  slackDays: null, infeasible: false,\n}));\nwriteFileSync('gantt-repro.svg', renderSvg(rows, opts, start));\nJS\nenv -i PATH=\"$PATH\" HOME=\"$REPRO_HOME\" XDG_CACHE_HOME=\"$REPRO_HOME/.cache\" \\\n  inkscape gantt-repro.svg --export-type=png --export-filename=gantt-repro.png\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom PIL import Image\nim = Image.open('gantt-repro.png').convert('RGB')\ncolors = Counter(im.getdata())\nprint('size:', im.size, 'unique RGB colors:', len(colors))\nprint('most common:', colors.most_common(3))\nassert len(colors) > 1, 'The whole chart rasterized to a single color'\nPY\n```\n\n`renderSvg` is an actual named export in both the current source and `dist/index.d.ts`. This fixture is fully synthetic; no tracker initialization or SDK reads are required by the renderer.\n\nActual with Inkscape `1.4 (e7c3feb100, 2024-10-09)`:\n\n```text\nsize: (576, 480) unique RGB colors: 1\nmost common: [((0, 0, 0), 276480)]\n```\n\nThe output PNG is entirely black. Inkscape returns success, with unsupported-CSS parsing warnings. Running the same reproduction on the base commit yields a legible 422×312 PNG with 632 RGB colors. Both images were visually inspected as well as pixel-counted.\n\n## Expected and acceptance\n\nStandalone SVG exports should remain readable when imported or converted in an ordinary desktop SVG consumer. Keep literal presentation-attribute colors for consumers without CSS-variable support, with optional CSS overrides for capable browser renderers. Adding a fallback argument inside `var()` alone will not help a consumer that does not implement `var()`.\n\nAdd a non-browser rendering check: the five-status fixture must retain a visible paper background, text, status fills and outlines in Inkscape 1.4, while existing light/dark browser checks continue to pass.\n\n## Verification scope\n\nThe exact base/head pure renderer implementations were exercised against Inkscape on synthetic rows, with isolated HOME, TZ=UTC and tracking disabled. The public named export and argument shape above were verified in current source/declarations; the full package build/SDK-backed import was not executed during this focused review. No live tracker, Core command, paid API or broad test suite was used. Chrome-only coverage cannot detect this consumer regression.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T03:45:23Z)\n>\n> Fixed in PR 152 at `d86b87d2d9c41f7be1015c33fc8168e4c2adbb41`. SVG now emits literal fill/stroke attributes and a self-contained literal-colour light/dark stylesheet, so native paint does not depend on CSS custom properties. Token-like item text is preserved.\n> \n> Regression: `standalone SVG retains literal paper, ink and status paints in a non-browser rasterizer`. It rasterizes all five states through resvg 2.6.2, requires exact solid paper/sheet/canary/rose fills and visible ink/stamp pixels (edge antialiasing allowed), and rejects unresolved paint variables. Native Inkscape/rsvg-convert are unavailable. `node --test test/svg.test.ts test/triplicate-visuals.test.ts` passes 22/22. `node test/revert-triplicate.ts --portable` restores only the old renderSvg function: 1/1 fails; restored implementation passes 1/1. Both-theme browser captures at 1440/768/390 pass at 1x/2x with zero overflow, animations, interactive actions or external requests. The PR embeds screenshots and the independent native PNG. Final tracker head `83f82037097e7756a759024549ef1d75193bb719` passes [CI run 39095108973](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/actions/runs/39095108973): full npm and Bun release gates each pass 250/250 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations/TODOs and 100% lines/branches/functions. Node 22.18 and 26 checks pass. The item remains in progress and unclaimed; no merge or package release was performed."
